{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/80837-gmc-and-revamping-contracts","id":80837,"title":"GMC and Revamping contracts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-26T23:34:07-08:00","id":80837,"title":"GMC and Revamping contracts","content":"So since there's like a year or two before we get a full revamp and I have a game going up now I decided to just start making a homebrew change.<br /> <br /> So I started with contracts first. Specifically dreams. Which in all honest. Was stupid. No one is taking it but you live and you learn. So I changed a few things and have a different approach to it. But as to the design philosophy. Narrow contracts are cool but the problem is when you have situations like Goblin contracts dealing with dreams when you have a Contract dealing with dreams there is a problem. So when dealing with something so broad it would be better to treat each contract as a mini arcana. Granted, I think clauses should still be purchased individually but they shouldn't be limited to a five power, that's it approach. So this is a little more open ended. I also have my design considerations in the comments so it's clear why I went with what I went with and what I'm still unsure of. Still some criticism would be nice.<br /> <br /> Next one is probably going to be elements or spring. Since I'm going to be working on the contracts my group has.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1imV-XS4X9SBb1_0T6MKPvORUIcn52Xbf4CGpUa6lExk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...GpUa6lExk/edit</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T00:41:46-08:00","id":80867,"title":"","content":"Dreams bugs me as it is. I've never been able to work out exactly what the limits on Forging the Dream are meant to be, or how it interacts with Oneiromancy. The way it's worded makes it sound like a Clause that flat out lets you ignore and override all Oneiromancy and just do whatever the heck you want. Not to mention the fact that Pathfinder is, as you say in the document, completely unrelated. The fourth and fifth dots don't have anything to do with dreams either, and Phantasmal Bastion is literally the only one that seems to interact with the Oneiromancy rules later in the book. It's always struck me as the most poorly designed Contract in Changeling, which is really frustrating. Dreams are fantastic, but the Contracts of Dream don't really want to have anything to do with them.<br /> <br /> While I don't really agree with your design philosophy (I like Contracts being rigid, defined, and inflexible with a regimented order in the way you purchase them, because I feel it suits the nature of rules-based Fae magic), I far prefer a lot of what you've done to the original Contract. I do think I'd just remove Forging the Dream entirely, bump Dream Stride to a two dot power, and make the one dot power a Pathfinder-equivalent, but instead of facts about the Hedge it gives you facts about the dream/person you are in. This is mostly because Dream Stride appears a little good for a one dot Clause, and (as mentioned) because I really don't like Forging the Dream. Other than that, I quite like what you have there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T07:32:48-08:00","id":81020,"title":"","content":"You might be right. Forging the Dream though is just a quick easy power. It's more of a shortcut. Dream Stride is probably better as a two dot contract.<br /> <br /> My design philosophy is kind of different than the norm but with changelings. I feel like dreams, elements are so large you can do so much with them. That having five and relegating the rest to goblin contracts is a disservice. That said, the second idea was limiting the contracts to five but letting a changeling choose what five he or she wants. Allowing two changelings to have completely different end game abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T13:27:08-08:00","id":81202,"title":"","content":"I'll have to look at this in more detail later. I think for now though what it's missing is a clause that lets you physically enter and leave dreams. I.E. Jump into someone's head, skeinwalk (or have a pledge) half way around the world, and jump out again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T13:29:11-08:00","id":81203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/80837-gmc-and-revamping-contracts?p=81202#post81202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll have to look at this in more detail later. I think for now though what it's missing is a clause that lets you physically enter and leave dreams. I.E. Jump into someone's head, skeinwalk (or have a pledge) half way around the world, and jump out again.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be the old fifth dot (Which I put at four but didn't change it). I'd probably still keep it at four though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T14:00:57-08:00","id":81222,"title":"","content":"No, not quite. The old fifth dot teleported you from your bed* to next to whomever's dream you were in a the time. I'm talking about something that lets you physically enter dreams, you want to spend your whole life in a Dream Bastion hiding from the fae while using lucid dreaming to conjure up entertainments - you can do that. Teleporting would be just one of the many uses.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Technically speaking, it teleported you from the Hedge, which should be impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T14:10:09-08:00","id":81227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/80837-gmc-and-revamping-contracts?p=81222#post81222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, not quite. The old fifth dot teleported you from your bed* to next to whomever's dream you were in a the time. I'm talking about something that lets you physically enter dreams, you want to spend your whole life in a Dream Bastion hiding from the fae while using lucid dreaming to conjure up entertainments - you can do that. Teleporting would be just one of the many uses.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Technically speaking, it teleported you from the Hedge, which should be impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>My fifth dot does it. It's however more expensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T14:16:41-08:00","id":81232,"title":"","content":"Would you believe I didn't even notice that. I thought Dream Eating was the 5th dot. Still though, I don't like the Willpower Dot cost. The reason I wanted to physically entire Dreams is that they always seemed a bit detached from the rest of the game. I wanted to make physically travelling into dreams somewhat common, like trips into the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T14:23:56-08:00","id":81236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/80837-gmc-and-revamping-contracts?p=81232#post81232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you believe I didn't even notice that. I thought Dream Eating was the 5th dot. Still though, I don't like the Willpower Dot cost. The reason I wanted to physically entire Dreams is that they always seemed a bit detached from the rest of the game. I wanted to make physically travelling into dreams somewhat common, like trips into the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two five dot dream contracts. Costs a dot because it's powerful. Permanently turning yourself into a dream would essentially make you immortal. It's not something that you should just be able to casually do I could alter it to be temporary. That is an option but the current cost is because of the benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T14:47:21-08:00","id":81245,"title":"","content":"There's no reason why turning yourself into a dream creature has to make you immortal. I'd just treat it as being a normal physical being who happens to be inside someone else's dreams - that kind of weirdness seems right for Changeling.<br /> <br /> A willpower Dot cost and permanence encourages you to go live in dreams forever, which is probably a bad idea if the rest of the plot is outside dreams. Making it work like trips to the hedge - cheep, normal physical bodies and you stay as long as you want - lets you make both realms involved in your games. That should be the goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T15:18:00-08:00","id":81265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/80837-gmc-and-revamping-contracts?p=81245#post81245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no reason why turning yourself into a dream creature has to make you immortal. I'd just treat it as being a normal physical being who happens to be inside someone else's dreams - that kind of weirdness seems right for Changeling.<br /> <br /> A willpower Dot cost and permanence encourages you to go live in dreams forever, which is probably a bad idea if the rest of the plot is outside dreams. Making it work like trips to the hedge - cheep, normal physical bodies and you stay as long as you want - lets you make both realms involved in your games. That should be the goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose. I'll change it to work like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T20:19:48-08:00","id":81383,"title":"","content":"As The Kings Raven says, entering a dream seems like it should be fine as a fifth dot Contract. You just need to rule that it makes you take health damage from Oneiromachy instead of Willpower damage.<br /> <br /> It would change the defensive application of Phantasmal Bastion a little, but &quot;Temporary Health equal to Wyrd&quot; should still be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T02:16:32-08:00","id":81478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/80837-gmc-and-revamping-contracts?p=81383#post81383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As The Kings Raven says, entering a dream seems like it should be fine as a fifth dot Contract. You just need to rule that it makes you take health damage from Oneiromachy instead of Willpower damage.<br /> <br /> It would change the defensive application of Phantasmal Bastion a little, but &quot;Temporary Health equal to Wyrd&quot; should still be fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually already a power the difference was I made it permanent and gave them a bunch of benefits for it. That said I removed most the benefits and lowered the cost dramatically so it'd be a little more in useful in application. (","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}